/* Verse Games: THE WHOLE COUNSEL · Numbers chapters 1-5
   Verse text is filled/verified from the KJV by tools/fill-verses.js */
VG.registerBibleChapters("numbers", [
{n:1, name:"The Census", seal:{ref:"Numbers 1:54",verse:"And the children of Israel did according to all that the LORD commanded Moses, so did they."}, facts:["Did you know the census counted only men twenty years and older fit for war, 603,550 of them, which means the whole nation with women and children likely numbered over two million souls (Numbers 1:3, 46)?","Did you know Judah was the largest tribe at 74,600 men, more than double the smallest tribe, Manasseh, at 32,200 (Numbers 1:27, 35)?","Did you know the Levites were left out of the census entirely and given charge of the tabernacle instead, a tribe set apart for God's house rather than the battlefield (Numbers 1:47-53)?"], questions:[
{q:"When did the LORD give the command for the census?", options:["On the first day of the second month, in the second year after leaving Egypt","On the first day of the seventh month, in the fortieth year","At the foot of Mount Sinai, the week after the exodus","On the tenth day of the first month, at Kadesh"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 1:1",verse:"And the LORD spake unto Moses in the wilderness of Sinai, in the tabernacle of the congregation, on the first day of the second month, in the second year after they were come out of the land of Egypt, saying,", insight:"God ordered the nation before marching it; counting comes before moving, in God's army and in life."},
{q:"Where was Moses when the LORD spoke to him about the census?", options:["In the tabernacle of the congregation, in the wilderness of Sinai","On the top of Mount Horeb, alone","In the plains of Moab, by the Jordan","At the well of Beersheba"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 1:1",verse:"And the LORD spake unto Moses in the wilderness of Sinai, in the tabernacle of the congregation, on the first day of the second month, in the second year after they were come out of the land of Egypt, saying,", insight:"The command came from the tent of meeting; God numbers His people from the place of His presence."},
{q:"What did God command Moses to take?", options:["The sum of all the congregation of the children of Israel","A census of the cattle and the flocks","An offering of silver from every tribe","The names of the elders only"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 1:2",verse:"Take ye the sum of all the congregation of the children of Israel, after their families, by the house of their fathers, with the number of their names, every male by their polls;", insight:"God knows His people by name; being counted is being claimed."},
{q:"How old did a man have to be to be numbered?", options:["Twenty years old and upward","Thirty years old and upward","Twelve years old and upward","Fifty years old and upward"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 1:3",verse:"From twenty years old and upward, all that are able to go forth to war in Israel: thou and Aaron shall number them by their armies.", insight:"Twenty marked a man ready for war; God counts those fit for the fight."},
{q:"Who helped Moses number the people?", options:["Aaron, and a head man of every tribe","Joshua and Caleb alone","The seventy elders","The sons of Levi only"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 1:4",verse:"And with you there shall be a man of every tribe; every one head of the house of his fathers.", insight:"One man from every tribe; God shares His work across the whole family."},
{q:"Who was the prince of the tribe of Reuben?", options:["Elizur the son of Shedeur","Shelumiel the son of Zurishaddai","Nahshon the son of Amminadab","Eliab the son of Helon"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 1:5",verse:"And these are the names of the men that shall stand with you: of the tribe of Reuben; Elizur the son of Shedeur.", insight:"Reuben, the firstborn tribe, was named first; order in God's house is never random."},
{q:"Who was the prince of the tribe of Judah?", options:["Nahshon the son of Amminadab","Nethaneel the son of Zuar","Ahira the son of Enan","Abidan the son of Gideoni"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 1:7",verse:"Of Judah; Nahshon the son of Amminadab.", insight:"Nahshon of Judah; from this line the promised King would one day come."},
{q:"Who was the prince of Ephraim?", options:["Elishama the son of Ammihud","Gamaliel the son of Pedahzur","Ahiezer the son of Ammishaddai","Pagiel the son of Ocran"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 1:10",verse:"Of the children of Joseph: of Ephraim; Elishama the son of Ammihud: of Manasseh; Gamaliel the son of Pedahzur.", insight:"Joseph's younger son's tribe named before the elder; God's favor is not bound by birth order."},
{q:"Who was the prince of Dan?", options:["Ahiezer the son of Ammishaddai","Elizur the son of Shedeur","Nethaneel the son of Zuar","Eliab the son of Helon"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 1:14",verse:"Of Gad; Eliasaph the son of Deuel.", insight:"Even the far tribes had their prince; no tribe is beneath God's notice."},
{q:"Who was the prince of Naphtali?", options:["Ahira the son of Enan","Eliasaph the son of Deuel","Abidan the son of Gideoni","Shelumiel the son of Zurishaddai"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 1:15",verse:"Of Naphtali; Ahira the son of Enan.", insight:"Last named among the princes, yet fully counted; God leaves no one off His list."},
{q:"How many fighting men did Reuben number?", options:["Forty and six thousand and five hundred","Fifty and nine thousand and three hundred","Forty and five thousand six hundred and fifty","Thirty and five thousand and four hundred"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 1:21",verse:"Those that were numbered of them, even of the tribe of Reuben, were forty and six thousand and five hundred.", insight:"Forty-six thousand five hundred from the firstborn's tribe; every number in Scripture is a person to God."},
{q:"Which tribe was the largest in the census?", options:["Judah, with threescore and fourteen thousand and six hundred","Dan, with threescore and two thousand and seven hundred","Simeon, with fifty and nine thousand and three hundred","Issachar, with fifty and four thousand and four hundred"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 1:27",verse:"Those that were numbered of them, even of the tribe of Judah, were threescore and fourteen thousand and six hundred.", insight:"Judah led in number as it would lead in the march; God puts His strength where He plans His purpose."},
{q:"How many did Judah number?", options:["Threescore and fourteen thousand and six hundred","Threescore and two thousand and seven hundred","Fifty and seven thousand and four hundred","Forty and six thousand and five hundred"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 1:27",verse:"Those that were numbered of them, even of the tribe of Judah, were threescore and fourteen thousand and six hundred.", insight:"Seventy-four thousand six hundred; the royal tribe was already the strongest tribe."},
{q:"Which tribe was the smallest in the census?", options:["Manasseh, with thirty and two thousand and two hundred","Benjamin, with thirty and five thousand and four hundred","Ephraim, with forty thousand and five hundred","Asher, with forty and one thousand and five hundred"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 1:35",verse:"Those that were numbered of them, even of the tribe of Manasseh, were thirty and two thousand and two hundred.", insight:"Smallest did not mean least loved; God's counting is about belonging, not ranking."},
{q:"What was the total number of fighting men?", options:["Six hundred thousand and three thousand and five hundred and fifty","Five hundred thousand and fifty thousand","Seven hundred thousand exactly","Four hundred thousand and twenty thousand"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 1:46",verse:"Even all they that were numbered were six hundred thousand and three thousand and five hundred and fifty.", insight:"Six hundred three thousand, five hundred fifty; from seventy souls in Egypt to an army in the wilderness."},
{q:"Were the Levites numbered in this census?", options:["No, they were not numbered among the children of Israel","Yes, they were counted with Judah","Yes, they were counted last of all","No, because they had stayed in Egypt"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 1:47",verse:"But the Levites after the tribe of their fathers were not numbered among them.", insight:"Left out of the army, set apart for the sanctuary; being uncounted here was the highest honor."},
{q:"What charge did God give the Levites?", options:["To bear the tabernacle and minister unto it, camping round about it","To lead the armies of Israel into battle","To divide the spoil among the tribes","To judge disputes between the tribes"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 1:50",verse:"But thou shalt appoint the Levites over the tabernacle of testimony, and over all the vessels thereof, and over all things that belong to it: they shall bear the tabernacle, and all the vessels thereof; and they shall minister unto it, and shall encamp round about the tabernacle.", insight:"Bearers of the holy things instead of bearers of arms; some serve God with the sword sheathed."},
{q:"What happened to the stranger who came near the holy things?", options:["He was to be put to death","He was fined five shekels","He was made a servant of the Levites","He was sent out of the camp for a week"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 1:51",verse:"And when the tabernacle setteth forward, the Levites shall take it down: and when the tabernacle is to be pitched, the Levites shall set it up: and the stranger that cometh nigh shall be put to death.", insight:"Holiness has a boundary; God is approachable, but never casual."},
{q:"Where did every tribe pitch?", options:["Every man by his own camp, and every man by his own standard","Wherever the pillar of cloud stopped first","In one great circle without order","Around the camp of Judah only"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 1:52",verse:"And the children of Israel shall pitch their tents, every man by his own camp, and every man by his own standard, throughout their hosts.", insight:"Every man in his place; God's order keeps a crowd from becoming a mob."},
{q:"Why were the Levites camped around the tabernacle?", options:["That there be no wrath upon the congregation of the children of Israel","That they might guard the gold of Egypt","That the other tribes would envy them","That Moses would have them near at hand"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 1:53",verse:"But the Levites shall pitch round about the tabernacle of testimony, that there be no wrath upon the congregation of the children of Israel: and the Levites shall keep the charge of the tabernacle of testimony.", insight:"A buffer of holiness around God's house; God protects His people even from His own holiness."}
]},
{n:2, name:"The Camp", seal:{ref:"Numbers 2:34",verse:"And the children of Israel did according to all that the LORD commanded Moses: so they pitched by their standards, and so they set forward, every one after their families, according to the house of their fathers."}, facts:["Did you know the whole nation formed a living courtyard around the tabernacle, Judah on the east, Reuben on the south, Ephraim on the west, and Dan on the north, marching in the same order they camped (Numbers 2:3-31)?","Did you know the camp of Judah alone numbered 186,400 men, larger than the entire camps of Ephraim or Reuben (Numbers 2:9)?","Did you know the tribe of Dan marched 'hindmost with their standards,' the rearguard of the nation, watching the backs of over half a million fighting men (Numbers 2:31)?"], questions:[
{q:"By what did every man of Israel pitch?", options:["By his own standard, with the ensign of his father's house","By the tribe nearest the tabernacle","By the lot cast each morning","By the command of his captain"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 2:2",verse:"Every man of the children of Israel shall pitch by his own standard, with the ensign of their father’s house: far off about the tabernacle of the congregation shall they pitch.", insight:"Every man knew his place and his banner; belonging has an address in God's camp."},
{q:"Were the Levites numbered among these camps?", options:["No, they were not numbered among the children of Israel","Yes, they were counted with Dan","Yes, they were counted with Judah","No, because they had stayed in Egypt"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 2:33",verse:"But the Levites were not numbered among the children of Israel; as the LORD commanded Moses.", insight:"Not numbered for war, because they were numbered for worship; God keeps His own lists."},
{q:"Which tribe's standard pitched on the east side?", options:["Judah","Reuben","Ephraim","Dan"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 2:3",verse:"And on the east side toward the rising of the sun shall they of the standard of the camp of Judah pitch throughout their armies: and Nahshon the son of Amminadab shall be captain of the children of Judah.", insight:"Judah faced the sunrise; the tribe of the coming Lion led the march toward the dawn."},
{q:"Which tribe pitched next to Judah on the east?", options:["Issachar","Simeon","Manasseh","Asher"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 2:5",verse:"And those that do pitch next unto him shall be the tribe of Issachar: and Nethaneel the son of Zuar shall be captain of the children of Issachar.", insight:"Next to Judah stood Issachar; strong tribes are stronger with faithful neighbors."},
{q:"How many were numbered in the camp of Judah?", options:["An hundred thousand and fourscore thousand and six thousand and four hundred","An hundred thousand and fifty and one thousand and four hundred and fifty","An hundred thousand and eight thousand and an hundred","An hundred thousand and fifty and seven thousand and six hundred"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 2:9",verse:"All that were numbered in the camp of Judah were an hundred thousand and fourscore thousand and six thousand and four hundred, throughout their armies. These shall first set forth.", insight:"One hundred eighty-six thousand four hundred; the largest camp led the way."},
{q:"Which camp set forth first on the march?", options:["The camp of Judah","The camp of Reuben","The camp of Ephraim","The camp of Dan"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 2:9",verse:"All that were numbered in the camp of Judah were an hundred thousand and fourscore thousand and six thousand and four hundred, throughout their armies. These shall first set forth.", insight:"First to pitch, first to march; leadership in God's order is a position, not a prize."},
{q:"Which tribe's standard was on the south side?", options:["Reuben","Judah","Ephraim","Dan"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 2:10",verse:"On the south side shall be the standard of the camp of Reuben according to their armies: and the captain of the children of Reuben shall be Elizur the son of Shedeur.", insight:"Reuben on the south; the firstborn's tribe kept an honored place though the birthright had passed."},
{q:"Which tribe pitched next to Reuben on the south?", options:["Simeon","Issachar","Manasseh","Asher"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 2:12",verse:"And those which pitch by him shall be the tribe of Simeon: and the captain of the children of Simeon shall be Shelumiel the son of Zurishaddai.", insight:"Simeon stood with Reuben; brothers camp together even when honors shift."},
{q:"How many were numbered in the camp of Reuben?", options:["An hundred thousand and fifty and one thousand and four hundred and fifty","An hundred thousand and fourscore thousand and six thousand and four hundred","An hundred thousand and eight thousand and an hundred","An hundred thousand and fifty and seven thousand and six hundred"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 2:16",verse:"All that were numbered in the camp of Reuben were an hundred thousand and fifty and one thousand and four hundred and fifty, throughout their armies. And they shall set forth in the second rank.", insight:"One hundred fifty-one thousand four hundred fifty; every camp was an army in itself."},
{q:"In what rank did the camp of Reuben set forth?", options:["The second rank","The first rank","The third rank","The hindmost"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 2:16",verse:"All that were numbered in the camp of Reuben were an hundred thousand and fifty and one thousand and four hundred and fifty, throughout their armies. And they shall set forth in the second rank.", insight:"Second, not first; faithfulness in the second rank is still faithfulness."},
{q:"Where did the tabernacle set forward in the march?", options:["In the midst of the camp","Ahead of the camp of Judah","Behind the camp of Dan","Beside the camp of Reuben"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 2:17",verse:"Then the tabernacle of the congregation shall set forward with the camp of the Levites in the midst of the camp: as they encamp, so shall they set forward, every man in his place by their standards.", insight:"God in the middle of His people; the march had a holy center."},
{q:"How were they to set forward?", options:["As they encamp, so shall they set forward, every man in his place","All together in one body","The Levites first, then the tribes","Each man as he pleased"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 2:17",verse:"Then the tabernacle of the congregation shall set forward with the camp of the Levites in the midst of the camp: as they encamp, so shall they set forward, every man in his place by their standards.", insight:"March as you camp; order on the road grows from order at rest."},
{q:"Which tribe's standard was on the west side?", options:["Ephraim","Judah","Reuben","Dan"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 2:18",verse:"On the west side shall be the standard of the camp of Ephraim according to their armies: and the captain of the sons of Ephraim shall be Elishama the son of Ammihud.", insight:"Ephraim on the west; Joseph's son held the sunset side of the camp."},
{q:"Which tribe pitched next to Ephraim on the west?", options:["Manasseh","Issachar","Gad","Naphtali"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 2:20",verse:"And by him shall be the tribe of Manasseh: and the captain of the children of Manasseh shall be Gamaliel the son of Pedahzur.", insight:"Manasseh beside Ephraim; Joseph's two sons kept the west together."},
{q:"How many were numbered in the camp of Ephraim?", options:["An hundred thousand and eight thousand and an hundred","An hundred thousand and fourscore thousand and six thousand and four hundred","An hundred thousand and fifty and one thousand and four hundred and fifty","An hundred thousand and fifty and seven thousand and six hundred"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 2:24",verse:"All that were numbered of the camp of Ephraim were an hundred thousand and eight thousand and an hundred, throughout their armies. And they shall go forward in the third rank.", insight:"One hundred eight thousand one hundred; the smallest camp, still mightier than Egypt's host."},
{q:"In what rank did the camp of Ephraim go forward?", options:["The third rank","The first rank","The second rank","The hindmost"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 2:24",verse:"All that were numbered of the camp of Ephraim were an hundred thousand and eight thousand and an hundred, throughout their armies. And they shall go forward in the third rank.", insight:"Third in rank, first in promise; Joseph's blessing outran its position."},
{q:"Which tribe's standard was on the north side?", options:["Dan","Judah","Reuben","Ephraim"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 2:25",verse:"The standard of the camp of Dan shall be on the north side by their armies: and the captain of the children of Dan shall be Ahiezer the son of Ammishaddai.", insight:"Dan on the north; the rearguard held the coldest quarter."},
{q:"Which tribe pitched next to Dan on the north?", options:["Asher","Zebulun","Simeon","Gad"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 2:27",verse:"And those that encamp by him shall be the tribe of Asher: and the captain of the children of Asher shall be Pagiel the son of Ocran.", insight:"Asher stood with Dan; the north side was guarded by brothers."},
{q:"How many were numbered in the camp of Dan?", options:["An hundred thousand and fifty and seven thousand and six hundred","An hundred thousand and fourscore thousand and six thousand and four hundred","An hundred thousand and fifty and one thousand and four hundred and fifty","An hundred thousand and eight thousand and an hundred"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 2:31",verse:"All they that were numbered in the camp of Dan were an hundred thousand and fifty and seven thousand and six hundred. They shall go hindmost with their standards.", insight:"One hundred fifty-seven thousand six hundred; the rearguard was no weakling."},
{q:"Which camp went hindmost?", options:["The camp of Dan, with their standards","The camp of Judah","The camp of Reuben","The camp of Ephraim"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 2:31",verse:"All they that were numbered in the camp of Dan were an hundred thousand and fifty and seven thousand and six hundred. They shall go hindmost with their standards.", insight:"Dan went hindmost; the last in line guarded the backs of a million people."}
]},
{n:3, name:"The Levites Numbered", seal:{ref:"Numbers 3:45",verse:"Take the Levites instead of all the firstborn among the children of Israel, and the cattle of the Levites instead of their cattle; and the Levites shall be mine: I am the LORD."}, facts:["Did you know God took the Levites in place of Israel's firstborn because He had claimed every firstborn on the night He struck Egypt's firstborn, 22,000 Levites standing in for 22,273 firstborn sons (Numbers 3:12-13, 39, 43)?","Did you know Nadab and Abihu, Aaron's eldest sons, died for offering 'strange fire' before the LORD, and because they had no children, the priesthood passed to Eleazar and Ithamar (Numbers 3:4)?","Did you know the 273 firstborn who outnumbered the Levites were redeemed at five shekels apiece, and Moses gave the money to Aaron and his sons (Numbers 3:46-51)?"], questions:[
{q:"Whose generations open this chapter?", options:["The generations of Aaron and Moses","The generations of Joshua and Caleb","The generations of the twelve tribes","The generations of Levi only"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 3:1",verse:"These also are the generations of Aaron and Moses in the day that the LORD spake with Moses in mount Sinai.", insight:"Aaron and Moses head the record; the Levites' story begins with the two brothers God used most."},
{q:"What were the names of Aaron's sons?", options:["Nadab, Abihu, Eleazar, and Ithamar","Nadab, Abihu, Gershon, and Merari","Eleazar, Ithamar, Amram, and Uzziel","Nadab, Eleazar, Phinehas, and Ithamar"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 3:2",verse:"And these are the names of the sons of Aaron; Nadab the firstborn, and Abihu, Eleazar, and Ithamar.", insight:"Four sons named; two would fall, two would carry the priesthood forward."},
{q:"What happened to Nadab and Abihu?", options:["They died when they offered strange fire before the LORD","They were made high priests in Aaron's place","They led the rebellion of Korah","They died of old age in the wilderness"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 3:4",verse:"And Nadab and Abihu died before the LORD, when they offered strange fire before the LORD, in the wilderness of Sinai, and they had no children: and Eleazar and Ithamar ministered in the priest’s office in the sight of Aaron their father.", insight:"Strange fire cost them their lives; God is not served with inventions of our own."},
{q:"Did Nadab and Abihu have children?", options:["No, they had no children","Yes, two sons each","Yes, but they were disinherited","The record does not say"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 3:4",verse:"And Nadab and Abihu died before the LORD, when they offered strange fire before the LORD, in the wilderness of Sinai, and they had no children: and Eleazar and Ithamar ministered in the priest’s office in the sight of Aaron their father.", insight:"No children; their line ended with their disobedience, a solemn warning."},
{q:"What were Aaron's sons consecrated to do?", options:["To minister in the priest's office","To lead the armies of Israel","To judge between the tribes","To carry the ark of the covenant"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 3:3",verse:"These are the names of the sons of Aaron, the priests which were anointed, whom he consecrated to minister in the priest’s office.", insight:"Anointed and consecrated; priesthood is God's appointment, not man's ambition."},
{q:"What did God command Moses to do with the tribe of Levi?", options:["Bring them near and present them before Aaron, that they may minister unto him","Number them for war with the other tribes","Send them back to Egypt","Give them the first portion of the land"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 3:6",verse:"Bring the tribe of Levi near, and present them before Aaron the priest, that they may minister unto him.", insight:"Brought near to minister; the Levites' calling was closeness, not conquest."},
{q:"What service did the Levites keep?", options:["The charge of the whole congregation, to do the service of the tabernacle","The treasury of the gold of Egypt","The armory of Israel's weapons","The records of the census"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 3:7",verse:"And they shall keep his charge, and the charge of the whole congregation before the tabernacle of the congregation, to do the service of the tabernacle.", insight:"Keepers of the charge; faithfulness in assigned service is true greatness."},
{q:"Who alone was appointed to the priest's office?", options:["Aaron and his sons","Moses and Aaron together","All the tribe of Levi","The princes of the tribes"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 3:10",verse:"And thou shalt appoint Aaron and his sons, and they shall wait on their priest’s office: and the stranger that cometh nigh shall be put to death.", insight:"Priesthood was not open to all; some callings are fenced by God's own command."},
{q:"Why did God take the Levites for Himself?", options:["Instead of all the firstborn among the children of Israel","Because they were the largest tribe","Because Moses asked for them","Because they volunteered first"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 3:12",verse:"And I, behold, I have taken the Levites from among the children of Israel instead of all the firstborn that openeth the matrix among the children of Israel: therefore the Levites shall be mine;", insight:"Taken instead of the firstborn; every Levite was a living reminder of the night of the Passover."},
{q:"When did God claim the firstborn?", options:["On the day He smote all the firstborn in the land of Egypt","At the crossing of the Red Sea","When the law was given at Sinai","At the building of the tabernacle"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 3:13",verse:"Because all the firstborn are mine; for on the day that I smote all the firstborn in the land of Egypt I hallowed unto me all the firstborn in Israel, both man and beast: mine shall they be: I am the LORD.", insight:"The night Egypt's firstborn died, Israel's firstborn became God's; judgment on one house is mercy on another."},
{q:"From what age were the Levite males numbered?", options:["From a month old and upward","From twenty years old and upward","From thirty years old and upward","From eight days old"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 3:15",verse:"Number the children of Levi after the house of their fathers, by their families: every male from a month old and upward shalt thou number them.", insight:"From a month old; even infants were counted in God's portion."},
{q:"What were the names of Levi's three sons?", options:["Gershon, Kohath, and Merari","Libni, Shimei, and Amram","Amram, Izehar, and Uzziel","Mahli, Mushi, and Zuriel"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 3:17",verse:"And these were the sons of Levi by their names; Gershon, and Kohath, and Merari.", insight:"Three sons, three families, three assignments; God divides the work but unites the purpose."},
{q:"How many Gershonites were numbered?", options:["Seven thousand and five hundred","Eight thousand and six hundred","Six thousand and two hundred","Twenty and two thousand"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 3:22",verse:"Those that were numbered of them, according to the number of all the males, from a month old and upward, even those that were numbered of them were seven thousand and five hundred.", insight:"Seven thousand five hundred keepers of the curtains; no task in God's house is small."},
{q:"Where did the families of Gershon pitch?", options:["Behind the tabernacle westward","On the south side","On the north side","Before the tabernacle eastward"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 3:23",verse:"The families of the Gershonites shall pitch behind the tabernacle westward.", insight:"Westward behind the tabernacle; every family had its appointed side."},
{q:"What was the charge of the sons of Gershon?", options:["The tabernacle, the tent, the covering, the hangings, and the cords","The ark and the mercy seat","The boards and the pillars","The altars and their vessels"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 3:25",verse:"And the charge of the sons of Gershon in the tabernacle of the congregation shall be the tabernacle, and the tent, the covering thereof, and the hanging for the door of the tabernacle of the congregation,", insight:"Keepers of the coverings; those who handle the curtains guard the glory within."},
{q:"How many Kohathites were numbered?", options:["Eight thousand and six hundred","Seven thousand and five hundred","Six thousand and two hundred","Two thousand seven hundred and fifty"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 3:28",verse:"In the number of all the males, from a month old and upward, were eight thousand and six hundred, keeping the charge of the sanctuary.", insight:"Eight thousand six hundred; the largest Levite family bore the holiest burden."},
{q:"What was the charge of the sons of Kohath?", options:["The ark, the table, the candlestick, the altars, and the vessels","The curtains and coverings","The boards, bars, and pillars","The outer court and its hangings"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 3:31",verse:"And their charge shall be the ark, and the table, and the candlestick, and the altars, and the vessels of the sanctuary wherewith they minister, and the hanging, and all the service thereof.", insight:"The ark, the table, the lampstand; the Kohathites carried the very presence of God."},
{q:"How many Merarites were numbered?", options:["Six thousand and two hundred","Seven thousand and five hundred","Eight thousand and six hundred","Three thousand and two hundred"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 3:34",verse:"And those that were numbered of them, according to the number of all the males, from a month old and upward, were six thousand and two hundred.", insight:"Six thousand two hundred; the frame-bearers of the tabernacle."},
{q:"How many firstborn males of Israel were numbered?", options:["Twenty and two thousand two hundred and threescore and thirteen","Twenty and two thousand exactly","Twenty and three thousand","Twenty and one thousand five hundred"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 3:43",verse:"And all the firstborn males by the number of names, from a month old and upward, of those that were numbered of them, were twenty and two thousand two hundred and threescore and thirteen.", insight:"Twenty-two thousand two hundred seventy-three; two hundred seventy-three more than the Levites who stood in for them."},
{q:"To whom did Moses give the redemption money?", options:["Unto Aaron and to his sons","Unto the princes of the tribes","Into the treasury of the tabernacle","Unto the firstborn themselves"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 3:51",verse:"And Moses gave the money of them that were redeemed unto Aaron and to his sons, according to the word of the LORD, as the LORD commanded Moses.", insight:"To Aaron and his sons, as the LORD commanded; God's accounts are settled exactly."}
]},
{n:4, name:"The Service of the Levites", seal:{ref:"Numbers 4:49",verse:"According to the commandment of the LORD they were numbered by the hand of Moses, every one according to his service, and according to his burden: thus were they numbered of him, as the LORD commanded Moses."}, facts:["Did you know the Kohathites carried the ark, the table, the lampstand, and the altars, but Aaron's sons had to wrap every holy thing first, because a Kohathite who touched or even looked at the uncovered vessels would die (Numbers 4:5, 15, 20)?","Did you know the ark traveled under three layers: the veil, then badgers' skins, then a cloth wholly of blue, heaven's color over the throne of God (Numbers 4:5-6)?","Did you know the Merarites' heavy load of boards, bars, pillars, and sockets was assigned 'by name,' every piece reckoned to a particular man (Numbers 4:32)?"], questions:[
{q:"From what age were the Levites counted for service?", options:["From thirty years old and upward even until fifty years old","From twenty years old and upward","From a month old and upward","From fifty years old and upward"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 4:3",verse:"From thirty years old and upward even until fifty years old, all that enter into the host, to do the work in the tabernacle of the congregation.", insight:"Thirty to fifty, the prime of strength; God claims the best years for the heaviest holy work."},
{q:"Whose service is described first?", options:["The sons of Kohath, about the most holy things","The sons of Gershon","The sons of Merari","The sons of Aaron"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 4:4",verse:"This shall be the service of the sons of Kohath in the tabernacle of the congregation, about the most holy things:", insight:"The Kohathites carried the most holy things; the nearer the glory, the heavier the care."},
{q:"Who covered the holy vessels before the camp moved?", options:["Aaron and his sons","The sons of Kohath","Eleazar alone","The princes of the tribes"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 4:5",verse:"And when the camp setteth forward, Aaron shall come, and his sons, and they shall take down the covering vail, and cover the ark of testimony with it:", insight:"Aaron's sons covered first; holy things are prepared by priests before they are carried by Levites."},
{q:"What first covered the ark of testimony?", options:["The covering vail","A cloth wholly of blue","A covering of badgers' skins","A cloth of scarlet"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 4:5",verse:"And when the camp setteth forward, Aaron shall come, and his sons, and they shall take down the covering vail, and cover the ark of testimony with it:", insight:"The veil that hid the glory covered the ark; reverence wraps what it cannot fully see."},
{q:"What went over the badgers' skins on the ark?", options:["A cloth wholly of blue","A cloth of scarlet","A cloth of purple","A cloth of fine linen"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 4:6",verse:"And shall put thereon the covering of badgers’ skins, and shall spread over it a cloth wholly of blue, and shall put in the staves thereof.", insight:"Blue over the ark, the color of heaven over the throne of God."},
{q:"What was spread upon the table of shewbread?", options:["A cloth of blue","A cloth of scarlet","A cloth of purple","A cloth of white linen"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 4:7",verse:"And upon the table of shewbread they shall spread a cloth of blue, and put thereon the dishes, and the spoons, and the bowls, and covers to cover withal: and the continual bread shall be thereon:", insight:"Blue first upon the table; even the bread of God's presence traveled in heaven's color."},
{q:"What came between the blue cloth and the badgers' skins on the table?", options:["A cloth of scarlet","A cloth of purple","A veil of fine linen","A net of brass"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 4:8",verse:"And they shall spread upon them a cloth of scarlet, and cover the same with a covering of badgers’ skins, and shall put in the staves thereof.", insight:"Scarlet between blue and skin; layers of care for the table that never lacked bread."},
{q:"What covered the candlestick of the light?", options:["A cloth of blue, then a covering of badgers' skins","A cloth of scarlet only","A veil of the temple","A purple cloth with staves"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 4:9",verse:"And they shall take a cloth of blue, and cover the candlestick of the light, and his lamps, and his tongs, and his snuffdishes, and all the oil vessels thereof, wherewith they minister unto it:", insight:"The lampstand that lit the holy place traveled wrapped in blue; light itself was handled with care."},
{q:"How was the candlestick carried?", options:["Put within badgers' skins and set upon a bar","Carried uncovered by two men","Hung from the staves of the ark","Wrapped in the covering veil"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 4:10",verse:"And they shall put it and all the vessels thereof within a covering of badgers’ skins, and shall put it upon a bar.", insight:"Upon a bar, borne by men; God's light moves on human shoulders."},
{q:"What covered the golden altar?", options:["A cloth of blue, covered with badgers' skins","A cloth of scarlet","The covering veil","A purple cloth"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 4:11",verse:"And upon the golden altar they shall spread a cloth of blue, and cover it with a covering of badgers’ skins, and shall put to the staves thereof:", insight:"Blue over the altar of incense; prayer itself was wrapped in heaven's color."},
{q:"What color cloth was spread on the altar of burnt offering?", options:["Purple","Blue","Scarlet","White"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 4:13",verse:"And they shall take away the ashes from the altar, and spread a purple cloth thereon:", insight:"Purple on the brazen altar; royalty marked the place of sacrifice."},
{q:"What would happen if the Kohathites touched the holy things?", options:["They would die","They would be made priests","They would be blessed","They would be sent out of the camp"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 4:15",verse:"And when Aaron and his sons have made an end of covering the sanctuary, and all the vessels of the sanctuary, as the camp is to set forward; after that, the sons of Kohath shall come to bear it: but they shall not touch any holy thing, lest they die. These things are the burden of the sons of Kohath in the tabernacle of the congregation.", insight:"Touch and die; nearness to God is not the same as casualness with God."},
{q:"What was committed to Eleazar the son of Aaron?", options:["The oil for the light, the sweet incense, the daily meat offering, and the anointing oil","The ark and the mercy seat","The silver trumpets","The books of the law"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 4:16",verse:"And to the office of Eleazar the son of Aaron the priest pertaineth the oil for the light, and the sweet incense, and the daily meat offering, and the anointing oil, and the oversight of all the tabernacle, and of all that therein is, in the sanctuary, and in the vessels thereof.", insight:"Eleazar kept the oil, the incense, the offering; the priest's son tended the daily worship."},
{q:"What were the Kohathites forbidden to do?", options:["To go in to see when the holy things are covered, lest they die","To bear the ark at all","To enter the court of the tabernacle","To speak the name of the LORD"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 4:20",verse:"But they shall not go in to see when the holy things are covered, lest they die.", insight:"Not even a look at the uncovered holy things; curiosity has no rights before glory."},
{q:"How many Gershonites were numbered for service?", options:["Two thousand and six hundred and thirty","Two thousand seven hundred and fifty","Three thousand and two hundred","Eight thousand and five hundred and fourscore"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 4:40",verse:"Even those that were numbered of them, throughout their families, by the house of their fathers, were two thousand and six hundred and thirty.", insight:"Two thousand six hundred thirty; the curtain-bearers in their strength."},
{q:"What did the sons of Gershon bear?", options:["The curtains of the tabernacle, its coverings, hangings, and cords","The ark and the altars","The boards and pillars","The vessels of the sanctuary"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 4:25",verse:"And they shall bear the curtains of the tabernacle, and the tabernacle of the congregation, his covering, and the covering of the badgers’ skins that is above upon it, and the hanging for the door of the tabernacle of the congregation,", insight:"Curtains and cords; the Gershonites carried the skin of God's house."},
{q:"Under whose hand was the service of Gershon?", options:["Ithamar the son of Aaron the priest","Eleazar the son of Aaron","Moses the man of God","Aaron himself"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 4:28",verse:"This is the service of the families of the sons of Gershon in the tabernacle of the congregation: and their charge shall be under the hand of Ithamar the son of Aaron the priest.", insight:"Under Ithamar's hand; every family of servants answers to an appointed overseer."},
{q:"How many Merarites were numbered for service?", options:["Three thousand and two hundred","Two thousand and six hundred and thirty","Two thousand seven hundred and fifty","Six thousand and two hundred"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 4:44",verse:"Even those that were numbered of them after their families, were three thousand and two hundred.", insight:"Three thousand two hundred; the heaviest timber trusted to the most numerous hands."},
{q:"What was the charge of the sons of Merari?", options:["The boards, bars, pillars, sockets, pins, and cords","The ark, table, and candlestick","The curtains and hangings","The oil and the incense"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 4:31",verse:"And this is the charge of their burden, according to all their service in the tabernacle of the congregation; the boards of the tabernacle, and the bars thereof, and the pillars thereof, and sockets thereof,", insight:"Boards and bars and sockets; the frame of God's house rested on Merarite shoulders."},
{q:"What was the total number of Levites in service?", options:["Eight thousand and five hundred and fourscore","Eight thousand and five hundred","Six thousand and two hundred","Twenty and two thousand"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 4:48",verse:"Even those that were numbered of them, were eight thousand and five hundred and fourscore.", insight:"Eight thousand five hundred eighty; a small army, wholly given to the worship of God."}
]},
{n:5, name:"Purity in the Camp", seal:{ref:"Numbers 5:28",verse:"And if the woman be not defiled, but be clean; then she shall be free, and shall conceive seed."}, facts:["Did you know the jealousy offering was barley meal with no oil and no frankincense, deliberately plain, because it was an offering 'bringing iniquity to remembrance' rather than a celebration (Numbers 5:15)?","Did you know Israel's restitution added a fifth on top of the principal, and if the wronged person had no kinsman, the payment went to the priest as unto the LORD Himself (Numbers 5:7-8)?","Did you know the bitter water ordeal protected the accused wife as much as it threatened her: if she was innocent she walked free and bore children, giving jealousy a courtroom instead of a knife (Numbers 5:28)?"], questions:[
{q:"Who was to be put out of the camp?", options:["Every leper, every one with an issue, and whoever was defiled by the dead","Every stranger in Israel","Every widow and orphan","Every man under twenty"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 5:2",verse:"Command the children of Israel, that they put out of the camp every leper, and every one that hath an issue, and whosoever is defiled by the dead:", insight:"Lepers, issues, the defiled by death; the camp of the living God kept death's shadows outside."},
{q:"Were both men and women put out?", options:["Yes, both male and female were put out","Only the men","Only the women","Only the priests"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 5:3",verse:"Both male and female shall ye put out, without the camp shall ye put them; that they defile not their camps, in the midst whereof I dwell.", insight:"Male and female alike; uncleanness does not respect persons, and neither does holiness."},
{q:"Why were they put outside the camp?", options:["That they defile not the camps, in the midst whereof God dwelt","To punish them for their sins","To make room for the Levites","To protect them from the plague"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 5:3",verse:"Both male and female shall ye put out, without the camp shall ye put them; that they defile not their camps, in the midst whereof I dwell.", insight:"God dwelt in the midst; purity in the camp flowed from Presence in the camp."},
{q:"Did the children of Israel obey?", options:["Yes, they did so, as the LORD spake unto Moses","No, they refused","They obeyed only in part","They waited forty years"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 5:4",verse:"And the children of Israel did so, and put them out without the camp: as the LORD spake unto Moses, so did the children of Israel.", insight:"They did so; obedience kept the camp clean and the conscience clear."},
{q:"What must a man or woman who sinned first do?", options:["Confess the sin which they have done","Offer a burnt offering at once","Leave the camp for seven days","Pay a fine to the elders"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 5:7",verse:"Then they shall confess their sin which they have done: and he shall recompense his trespass with the principal thereof, and add unto it the fifth part thereof, and give it unto him against whom he hath trespassed.", insight:"Confession first, then restitution; God heals the conscience before the account."},
{q:"How much was added to the restitution?", options:["The fifth part","The tenth part","Double","The half"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 5:7",verse:"Then they shall confess their sin which they have done: and he shall recompense his trespass with the principal thereof, and add unto it the fifth part thereof, and give it unto him against whom he hath trespassed.", insight:"The principal plus a fifth; true repentance pays more than it took."},
{q:"If the wronged man had no kinsman, to whom was the trespass paid?", options:["Unto the LORD, even to the priest","Unto the king","Unto the elders of the city","It was forgiven and forgotten"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 5:8",verse:"But if the man have no kinsman to recompense the trespass unto, let the trespass be recompensed unto the LORD, even to the priest; beside the ram of the atonement, whereby an atonement shall be made for him.", insight:"Paid to the priest as unto the LORD; when no man can be repaid, God receives the debt."},
{q:"What else was offered besides the restitution?", options:["The ram of the atonement","A lamb for a burnt offering","Two turtledoves","A tenth of an ephah of flour"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 5:8",verse:"But if the man have no kinsman to recompense the trespass unto, let the trespass be recompensed unto the LORD, even to the priest; beside the ram of the atonement, whereby an atonement shall be made for him.", insight:"A ram for atonement beside the payment; restitution settles with man, atonement settles with God."},
{q:"What offering did the jealous husband bring for his wife?", options:["The tenth part of an ephah of barley meal","A lamb without blemish","Two young pigeons","A tenth of wheat flour with oil"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 5:15",verse:"Then shall the man bring his wife unto the priest, and he shall bring her offering for her, the tenth part of an ephah of barley meal; he shall pour no oil upon it, nor put frankincense thereon; for it is an offering of jealousy, an offering of memorial, bringing iniquity to remembrance.", insight:"Barley meal, the poor man's grain; jealousy brings no rich offering."},
{q:"Why were no oil or frankincense put on the jealousy offering?", options:["For it was an offering of jealousy, bringing iniquity to remembrance","Because the priest had none","Because it was a sin offering for the priest","Because oil was reserved for kings"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 5:15",verse:"Then shall the man bring his wife unto the priest, and he shall bring her offering for her, the tenth part of an ephah of barley meal; he shall pour no oil upon it, nor put frankincense thereon; for it is an offering of jealousy, an offering of memorial, bringing iniquity to remembrance.", insight:"No oil, no frankincense; this was no celebration, but a memorial of suspected sin."},
{q:"What did the priest mix into the holy water?", options:["Dust from the floor of the tabernacle","Ashes from the altar","Salt from the Dead Sea","Oil from the olive press"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 5:17",verse:"And the priest shall take holy water in an earthen vessel; and of the dust that is in the floor of the tabernacle the priest shall take, and put it into the water:", insight:"Dust from the tabernacle floor in holy water; the bitter water carried the very ground of God's house."},
{q:"What did the priest do to the woman's head?", options:["He uncovered it","He anointed it with oil","He covered it with a veil","He placed ashes on it"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 5:18",verse:"And the priest shall set the woman before the LORD, and uncover the woman’s head, and put the offering of memorial in her hands, which is the jealousy offering: and the priest shall have in his hand the bitter water that causeth the curse:", insight:"Uncovered before the LORD; nothing hidden can stand in God's court."},
{q:"What was placed in the woman's hands?", options:["The offering of memorial, the jealousy offering","The bitter water","The book of the curses","A handful of barley"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 5:18",verse:"And the priest shall set the woman before the LORD, and uncover the woman’s head, and put the offering of memorial in her hands, which is the jealousy offering: and the priest shall have in his hand the bitter water that causeth the curse:", insight:"The memorial in her hands; she held the offering that would declare her."},
{q:"If the woman was innocent, what would the bitter water do?", options:["She would be free from the bitter water that caused the curse","It would make her ill for seven days","It would mark her forehead","It would bind her to silence"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 5:19",verse:"And the priest shall charge her by an oath, and say unto the woman, If no man have lain with thee, and if thou hast not gone aside to uncleanness with another instead of thy husband, be thou free from this bitter water that causeth the curse:", insight:"Innocence had nothing to fear from the bitter water; truth is the best defense."},
{q:"What would happen to the guilty woman?", options:["Her belly would swell and her thigh would rot","She would be stoned at once","She would be put out of the camp","She would pay a hundred shekels"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 5:27",verse:"And when he hath made her to drink the water, then it shall come to pass, that, if she be defiled, and have done trespass against her husband, that the water that causeth the curse shall enter into her, and become bitter, and her belly shall swell, and her thigh shall rot: and the woman shall be a curse among her people.", insight:"Belly to swell, thigh to rot; hidden sin writes its verdict on the body."},
{q:"What did the priest write?", options:["These curses in a book","The woman's name on the altar","The husband's oath on a stone","The law on the doorpost"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 5:23",verse:"And the priest shall write these curses in a book, and he shall blot them out with the bitter water:", insight:"Curses written in a book, then blotted out; even judgment can be washed away."},
{q:"With what did the priest blot out the curses?", options:["With the bitter water","With hyssop and blood","With oil","With the ashes of the offering"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 5:23",verse:"And the priest shall write these curses in a book, and he shall blot them out with the bitter water:", insight:"Blotted out with bitter water; the very water of judgment became the eraser."},
{q:"What did the woman answer to the oath?", options:["Amen, amen","I am innocent","Let it be so","The LORD is my witness"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 5:22",verse:"And this water that causeth the curse shall go into thy bowels, to make thy belly to swell, and thy thigh to rot: And the woman shall say, Amen, amen.", insight:"Amen, amen; she sealed the oath with her own mouth."},
{q:"If the woman was clean, what was promised?", options:["She would be free, and would conceive seed","She would be made a priestess","Her husband would pay her double","She would be crowned with honor"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 5:28",verse:"And if the woman be not defiled, but be clean; then she shall be free, and shall conceive seed.", insight:"Free, and would conceive seed; vindication ended not in shame but in fruitfulness."},
{q:"What is this law called?", options:["The law of jealousies","The law of the Nazirite","The law of the trespass offering","The law of purification"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 5:29",verse:"This is the law of jealousies, when a wife goeth aside to another instead of her husband, and is defiled;", insight:"The law of jealousies; God gave jealousy a courtroom instead of a knife."}
]}
]);
